  "description": "The 2026 election for Oklahoma's 4th Congressional District pits longtime incumbent Rep. Tom Cole (R) against two Democratic primary candidates and an independent candidate in the general election. The district covers south-central Oklahoma across 14 counties, including Norman, Lawton, Moore, Midwest City, and Ardmore. Cole, who has held the seat since 2003 and chairs the powerful House Appropriations Committee, faces a primary challenge from self-described America First candidate Marcie Everhart. The Democratic primary features retired Air Force Colonel Jeff Pixley and U.S. Army veteran and public defender Mitchell Jacob. Independent disability advocate Rocco Bonacci will also appear on the general election ballot. The primary elections are scheduled for June 16, 2026.",
